+## Explainable exception resolution (audit feature)
+
+A break resolution is proposed by one analyst (the *maker*), approved or rejected by a
+different person (the *checker*), and every step is written to an append-only, hash-chained
+history that Compliance can export for a business-date range. The reconciliation engine and
+its reports are untouched — the workflow is a separate host with its own state.
+
+### Adapter contract
+
+`audit-adapter.json` at the repository root is the data-only, shell-free contract. Every
+command is an `executable` plus an `arguments` array in which the evaluator substitutes the
+documented placeholders:
+
+| Command | Placeholders | Allowed exit codes |
+|---------|--------------|--------------------|
+| `initialize` | `{stateDirectory}` | `0` |
+| `propose` | `{stateDirectory}` `{requestId}` `{proposer}` `{businessDate}` `{reason}` `{evidence}` | `0`, `3` |
+| `decide` | `{stateDirectory}` `{requestId}` `{approver}` `{decision}` | `0`, `3` |
+| `export` | `{stateDirectory}` `{fromDate}` `{toDate}` `{exportPath}` | `0` |
+
+Every command prints exactly one deterministic JSON document to stdout; diagnostics go to
+stderr. `export` additionally writes the same document to `{exportPath}`. Exit code `0` means
+the outcome is durable (newly written or already present, i.e. idempotent), `3` means the
+command was refused by a workflow rule and nothing was written, and `1` is a usage or
+internal error.
+
+```powershell
+dotnet run --project src/TradeRecon.AuditConsole -c Release -- initialize --state ./state
+dotnet run --project src/TradeRecon.AuditConsole -c Release -- propose --state ./state `
+  --request-id req-1 --proposer maker-a --business-date 2024-06-03 `
+  --reason "custodian confirmed a timing difference" --evidence "ticket AUD-4471"
+dotnet run --project src/TradeRecon.AuditConsole -c Release -- decide --state ./state `
+  --request-id req-1 --approver checker-b --decision approve
+dotnet run --project src/TradeRecon.AuditConsole -c Release -- export --state ./state `
+  --from 2024-06-01 --to 2024-06-30 --export-path ./state/audit-history.json
+```
+
+`requestId` is caller-supplied and is preserved verbatim, so a harness may use a
+reconciliation `breakKey`, a ticket number or any other identifier.
+
+### Workflow guarantees
+
+1. **Maker–checker.** A terminal decision is only recorded when the checker identity differs
+   from the *durable* proposer identity loaded from the persisted proposal (comparison ignores
+   case and surrounding whitespace). Self-approval writes nothing and exits `3`.
+2. **Exactly one final decision.** Read-validate-append runs under an exclusive cross-process
+   lock (`{stateDirectory}/audit/.lock`), so concurrent approve and reject commands both
+   complete through declared outcomes while only one terminal entry becomes durable.
+3. **Idempotent retries.** Repeating an identical proposal or an identical accepted decision
+   returns `status: "idempotent"` with exit `0` and appends nothing.
+4. **Append-only and tamper-evident.** Entries are only ever appended to
+   `{stateDirectory}/audit/ledger.jsonl`. Each entry carries a contiguous 1-based `sequence`
+   and a `hash`/`previousHash` chain; `previousHash` is `null` for sequence 1 and otherwise
+   equals the preceding entry's `hash`.
+5. **No account or amount leakage.** Analyst free text is scrubbed before it is hashed and
+   persisted, so account-like tokens and monetary amounts cannot reach stdout, stderr, the
+   ledger or the export. A SHA-256 digest of the original text is retained so the evidence
+   remains verifiable.
+
+### Durable state
+
+```
+{stateDirectory}/audit/ledger.jsonl   append-only, one canonical JSON entry per line
+{stateDirectory}/audit/metadata.json  schema version and creation timestamp
+{stateDirectory}/audit/.lock          cross-process lock guarding conditional appends
+```
+
+State survives across separate command processes; any command creates the layout if
+`initialize` has not been run.
+
+### Export document
+
+```jsonc
+{
+  "schemaVersion": "1.0",
+  "command": "export",
+  "status": "completed",
+  "ok": true,
+  "fromDate": "2024-06-01",
+  "toDate": "2024-06-30",
+  "generatedAt": "2024-06-30T09:00:00.000Z",
+  "entryCount": 2,
+  "entries": [
+    {
+      "schemaVersion": "1.0",
+      "sequence": 1,
+      "requestId": "req-1",
+      "action": "PROPOSED",          // PROPOSED | APPROVED | REJECTED
+      "actor": "maker-a",
+      "actorRole": "proposer",       // proposer | checker
+      "proposer": "maker-a",
+      "checker": null,               // set on the terminal entry
+      "businessDate": "2024-06-03",
+      "reason": "custodian confirmed a timing difference",
+      "reasonDigest": "<sha256 of the original reason>",
+      "evidence": "ticket AUD-4471",
+      "evidenceDigest": "<sha256 of the original evidence>",
+      "redacted": false,
+      "recordedAt": "2024-06-03T18:04:11.512Z",
+      "previousHash": null,
+      "hash": "<sha256>"
+    }
+  ]
+}
+```
+
+Entries are selected by inclusive `businessDate` range and ordered by `sequence`. A decision
+inherits the business date of its proposal, so a request's history is never split across a
+range boundary.
+
+**Verifying an entry.** Remove the `hash` property, serialise the remaining object as compact
+JSON with object keys sorted recursively in code-point order, UTF-8 encode it, and take the
+lowercase hex SHA-256 digest. The result must equal `hash`, and `previousHash` must match the
+previous entry's `hash`.
+
